cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use barista in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "BARISTA: BARrier Inference of Sequential, Tunnelling and Activated transport"
abstract: >-
  BARISTA identifies the charge-transport mechanism across thin insulating, semiconducting,
  molecular or magnetic barriers from current-voltage data at one or more temperatures and
  thicknesses. It fits tunnelling, trap-assisted, hopping, emission and space-charge-limited
  mechanisms globally, ranks them with information criteria, cross-validation and plausibility
  checks, quantifies uncertainty by bootstrap and profile likelihood, extracts trap densities
  and energies, covers spin-dependent transport, and writes manuscript-ready figures, tables
  and Methods text.
type: software
